             Digital's 64-BIT AlphaServer 1000A System 
       Gets Enhanced Power, Flexible Packaging, Lower Pricing 


          ... Superior uniprocessor TPC-C performance ...
   ... Ideal for Internet, telephony, multimedia applications ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 6, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced significant performance and packaging enhancements 
as well as memory and upgrade price reductions for its AlphaServer 
1000A family of 64-bit uniprocessor RISC systems. 

     The new AlphaServer 1000A 5/300 system, supercharged with a 300 
MHz Alpha 21164 EV5 processor, is the most powerful, expandable, 
dependable, and easy-to-manage server in its class. The new systems 
are available now.

     In addition, the AlphaServer 1000A 5/300 systems are available 
either fully configured or as new distributor packages, which ship 
without operating system, memory, or disk. This design offers 
distribution partners configuration flexibility and improved 
inventory management.

     "The new AlphaServer powerhouse will help customers leapfrog 
their competitors by providing a dramatic boost in 64-bit 
performance to power their most dynamic, demanding applications, 
such as the Internet and intranets, decision support, computer 
telephony, and multimedia," said Nancy Epple, AlphaServer marketing 
director. "Digital continues to strengthen the entry-level AlphaServer 
line by adding many of the breakthrough features in our most powerful 
enterprise servers -- at little or no extra cost to customers."

     "Our popular distributor packages, available for the first time 
on the AlphaServer 1000 family, enhance VAR customer satisfaction, 
as well as our partners' profit margins," she added. 

Maintaining the Alpha Performance Lead 

     The new 300 MHz AlphaServer 1000A maintains performance and 
price/performance leadership of Alpha platforms on the most popular 
industry applications. 

     Audited TPC-C benchmark results of 1691 tpmC at $158/tpmC, 
running Digital UNIX, Sybase SQL Server 11.0, and BEA Tuxedo 
System/T V4.2, give the new 300 MHz AlphaServer 1000A 5/300 system 
the industry lead for single-processor TPC-C performance. It offers 
better price/performance than competitive uniprocessor systems such 
as the Compaq ProLiant 1500 5/166 and the Sun UltraServer1 Model 
170.  

     With 8.48 SPECint95, and 9.84 SPECfp95, the new system delivers 
unparalleled performance and value: nearly twice the SPECint95 
performance of the AlphaServer 1000A 4/266, 135% higher SPECint95 
performance than the 100 MHz PA7200-based HP 9000 D250 and D350 
systems, nearly double the SPECint95 performance of the Compaq 
ProLiant 1500 5/166 system, and 33% better SPECint95 performance 
than the Sun UltraServer1 Model 170. 

     The AlphaServer 1000A family provides the industry's best 
uniprocessor Internet performance and price/performance, based on 
SPECweb96, a standardized benchmark for measuring basic Web server 
performance.  The AlphaServer 1000A 4/266 system, with a SPECweb96 
result of 252, outperformed the Hewlett Packard D210 system, with a
SPECweb96 of 216. The AlphaServer system used only 128 MB of memory, 
compared with 416 MB in the HP system. The AlphaServer system ran Digital 
UNIX and Netscape Communications Server V1.12. For more information, 
refer to: http//www.specbench.org/osg/web96

Pricing and Availability

     AlphaServer 1000A 5/300 distributor packages, priced from 
$9,370, including Fast Ethernet adapter and CD-ROM, are available 
September 5. Fully configured systems, including the Windows NT 
operating system, 64 MB ECC memory, and 2 GB disk, are priced from 
$14,995. Rackmount systems, offering nearly unlimited configuration 
flexibility in a space-saving footprint, start at $10,350.

     Digital's award-winning Internet AlphaServer systems, which 
include popular Internet software, such as Netscape Communications 
Server, are priced from $18,975 for the new AlphaServer 1000A 5/300 
systems.

     To ensure continued investment protection and increased 
application performance, customers and business partners can upgrade 
their current AlphaServer 1000 and 1000A systems. For example, users 
of EV4 266 MHz AlphaServer 1000 and 1000A systems can upgrade to EV5 
300 MHz processors for less than $5,000. 

     Digital has reduced memory add-on prices for AlphaServer 1000A 
systems by more than 30 percent, to $50 per MB of ECC memory.  The 
company also lowered the entry price for AlphaServer 1000A 4/266 
systems to $9,995 for a Windows NT system with 32 MB of memory and 1 
GB disk.

Superior Performance, Expandability, Value

     The new AlphaServer 1000A 5/300 family offers the memory, 
storage capacity, and expandability typically available only in the 
high-end systems of other vendors: up to 1 GB ECC SIMM memory, up to 
2 MB ECC cache, maximum 30.1 GB internal disk storage, and more than 
400 GB maximum external. Nine industry-standard expansion slots 
(7 PCI, 2 EISA) enable connections to low-cost, high-performance 
options. Other features include a 128-bit CPU to memory bus 
bandwidth (533 MB/sec), integral Fast Wide Single-Ended SCSI, hot 
swappable disks, and redundant power supplies. Customers can choose 
Digital UNIX, Windows NT, or OpenVMS operating systems.

     All AlphaServer systems ship with Digital's ServerWORKS server 
management software and BMC PATROL software for application and 
database server management. Digital continues to offer its 
pace-setting three-year, on-site hardware warranty. 

     For more details see the AlphaServer Web site at 
http://www.digital.com/info/alphaserver

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
