      Digital Announces Storageworks Enterprise Storage Arrays;
          Open Solutions For The Growing Enterprise Market


    First in Series Of High-End Storage Products for Open Systems


MAYNARD, Mass., August 7, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today reinforced its position as the leader in the growing 
enterprise storage market with the introduction of the Enterprise 
Storage Array (ESA) to its StorageWorks product family.  

     Sized from just over 150 GB to more than 10 TB, the 
StorageWorks ESA products capitalize on Digital's leadership in 
64-bit computing. They deliver the highest levels of storage 
capacity, availability, flexibility, and performance for large, 
complex mission-critical applications.

     "The Enterprise Storage Arrays make it easy for our customers 
to understand,, compare, and implement large storage subsystems. Our 
channel partners benefit as well from the ease of configuration, and 
the ease of selling built into the product line. To date, we know of 
no other storage vendor who can provide a single subsystem with the 
capacity and performance to support 10 TB databases," said Kirby 
Wadsworth, Director of Storage Product Marketing for Digital.

     The growing popularity of data warehousing applications, 
on-line analytical processing (OLAP) and data mining is leading 
businesses to consolidate information storage in client/server 
environments, and is driving demand for enterprise-class storage 
that can be expanded easily without restrictions.  Analysts predict 
that the data warehousing application market alone will reach $8 
billion by 1998. Enterprise Storage Arrays offer a range of  
tailor-made storage solutions optimized for the intense demands of 
enterprise computing.

StorageWorks Innovative Architecture 

     The StorageWorks Enterprise Storage Arrays are based on 
Digital's innovative, award-winning StorageWorks architecture, and 
offer nearly limitless scalability. Increases in capacity are 
accompanied by parallel increases in performance. By incorporating 
the latest StorageWorks RAID controller technology, applications 
benefit from peak throughput, bandwidth, and continuous 
availability.

     "We expect StorageWorks to be a big part of our data warehouse 
efforts. It gives us the high availability and high throughput we 
need to run enterprise-level applications across platforms.  
StorageWorks ensures that critical patient, hospital and scheduling 
information is available to our staff when they need it," said Joe 
Furmanski, Technical Support Services Manager, University of 
Pittsburgh Medical Center. 

StorageWorks Enterprise Storage Arrays 

     Digital's Enterprise Storage Arrays, high-performance RAID 
subsystems tuned for different application work loads, are the first 
offerings in a series of Digital products aimed at the high-end open 
systems market. All Enterprise Storage Arrays offer RAID levels 0, 
1, 0+1, 3 and 5. All feature fully redundant components including 
power supplies and fans. Included with each array is StorageWorks 
Command Console software, an easy-to-use multiplatform configuration 
and management tool. The Command Console allows simple 
configuration, and provides at-a-glance summary status through a new 
easy-to-use graphical interface. Its fault isolation and reporting 
feature allows remote notification, escalation, and diagnosis in the 
event of a component failure.

     "Digital's new StorageWorks Enterprise Storage Arrays remove 
much of the pain of implementing large, complex, failure-tolerant 
arrays. By basing these new products on standard, highly modular 
components, Digital offers users a solid foundation for crafting 
scaleable, high-quality storage solutions," said Rick Westerman, 
Program Director, Europe, OCSS, META Group.

     StorageWorks Enterprise Storage Arrays will support multiple 
open systems platforms including Digital UNIX, HP, SUN, Windows NT, 
OpenVMS, IBM and other platforms. StorageWorks Enterprise Storage 
Arrays are available immediately.  Pricing starts at US$195,000 and 
includes on-site installation and setup.

     Enterprise Storage Arrays take full advantage of current 
application design, such as random mapping and host-based read 
cache. The dynamic mapping feature makes data available to the host 
cache far more quickly than the largest traditional sequential cache 
systems.

Oracle Warehouse Terabyte Test-to-Scale Certification

     Digital's multi-terabyte Enterprise Storage has been awarded 
Oracle Corp.'s Test-to-Scale certification. The subsystem is the 
first storage solution to demonstrate a RAID level 5, multi-terabyte 
configuration that meets data-warehousing requirements while 
offering higher availability and substantially lower cost per 
megabyte than RAID level 0+1 configurations.

     For more information about Digital's complete line of storage 
hardware and software products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) 
or visit http://www.storage.digital.com on the World Wide Web.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 

