          AltaVista Search in Major Worldwide Expansion --
        `Mirror' Sites Planned for Scandinavia and Australia


    Telia TeleCom AB of Sweden and Telstra of Australia to Become
         First Affiliates of the AltaVista WorldWide Network


MAYNARD, Mass., August 20, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today took a major step in establishing a worldwide network of 
`mirror' sites for AltaVista, with the announcement of plans to 
create regional Affiliate sites in northern Europe and Australia/New 
Zealand.  The first two Affiliates of the AltaVista WorldWide 
Network, Telia TeleCom AB of Sweden and Telstra/Yellow Pages of 
Australia, have signed letters of intent to establish local 
AltaVista sites that will provide users with faster access and 
quicker response to their Internet search queries.

     The AltaVista site in Scandinavia, to be located on the 
Internet at http://www.internet.telia.com, will primarily target 
Internet users in Scandinavia, the Baltics, Poland, Germany and 
Benelux. The AltaVista site in Australia, at 
http://www.altavista.yellowpages.com.au, will target users in 
Australia and New Zealand.   Both sites are planned to be 
operational in October, and Telia and Telstra/Yellow Pages will sell 
advertising space on their regional sites.  When complete, the AltaVista 
WorldWide Network will consist of up to a dozen sites in Europe, Asia, 
Africa, Australia and Latin America, managed by Affiliate partners 
in each country.  Affiliates will adapt the AltaVista search service to 
their local markets by translating the user interface and help pages 
into local languages.

     "With our planned rapid expansion and growth of the AltaVista 
WorldWide Network, we will offer far more users access to the 
service, and provide higher quality performance," said Ilene H. 
Lang, vice president of Digital's Internet Software Business Unit. 
"Both of our partners have invested significant resources into 
building a powerful infrastructure for the Internet, and we are 
proud to have them as our first AltaVista Affiliates." 

     "Accurate search results are becoming more and more important 
as the  Internet grows.  As AltaVista Search is one of the most 
attractive services in the global network, our partnership with 
Digital will be an important part of Telia's Internet business," 
said Tomas Duffy, general manager for Telia TeleCom AB.  "Along with 
our new network, Telia Internet, we will offer the capacity needed 
for delivering fast search results for all users in northern 
Europe."

     "AltaVista Search is one of the most attractive services in the 
global network," said Bob Copp, national multimedia manager for 
Telstra/Yellow Pages. "Internet users will be able to navigate 
around the Net at an unprecedented level of speed and performance, 
finding businesses through the yellow pages and telephone numbers 
through the white pages.  Yellow Pages and AltaVista will be the 
bridge joining millions of Internet users and our 300,000 
customers."

     Today, Digital's data center in Palo Alto, Calif. processes 
all queries to the AltaVista Search Service, located at 
http://altavista.digital.com. Responding to the rapid growth of 
Internet users from outside the United States, Digital is 
aggressively implementing plans to mirror the search service by 
establishing the AltaVista WorldWide Network.  Each Affiliate will 
use the identical search index, providing identical results to 
queries around the world.

     AltaVista software solutions from Digital provide high 
performance Internet connectivity to help cyberworkers quickly find 
useful information, easily communicate and collaborate over secure 
virtual networks.  The AltaVista family of products includes Private 
eXtensions, a search solution that is an extension from the 
AltaVista public search service on the Internet for finding 
information in corporate intranets, workgroups or on an individual's 
PC. Further information on AltaVista software solutions is available 
on the Worldwide Web at http://altavista.software.digital.com. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
