               Digital and Progressive Networks Boost
             Professional-Quality Audio on the Internet


 Progressive Networks' RealAudio Now Available on the Alpha Platform


MAYNARD, Mass., August 15, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, a 
leader in business-to-business solutions for open networks and the 
World Wide Web, announced today that Progressive Networks' 
RealAudio(tm) Server solution is now available on Digital's powerful 
Alpha platform for both Digital UNIX and Windows NT.  RealAudio 
delivers music-quality audio-on-demand over the Internet, including 
live cybercasts, concerts, and breaking news, and is featured on 
many popular Web sites today.  

     Many of today's breakthrough technologies come from small, 
innovative companies.  Digital is forging partnerships with many of 
them through its Internet Innovators program, which helps Internet 
software companies port to the 64-bit Alpha platform and promote the 
resulting product to Digital's international channel partners, 
customers and prospects.

     "We are pleased to have Progressive Networks and their 
award-winning RealAudio software as an Internet Innovators Partner," 
said Joan Jacobs, program director for Digital's Internet Business 
Group. "RealAudio and the Alpha platform are perfectly paired to 
deliver high-quality multimedia solutions to demanding Internet 
audiences, as well as for use in corporate communications and 
training."  

     Digital, a pioneer in the Internet/Intranet market, has also 
licensed RealAudio software for its internal and external Web sites. 
Digital is using RealAudio with PowerPoint slides to replace 
videotapes for internal training programs, making online training 
material available faster and at lower cost. "We are pleased with 
Digital's selection of RealAudio for use in their own corporate 
communications.  We believe Digital's expertise with RealAudio will 
be one more reason why Digital will be a leading provider of 
Intranet solutions," said Janet Lawless, director of strategic sales 
at Progressive Networks.  

     In addition to internal communications, companies face the 
challenge of attracting outside prospects to their Web sites and 
presenting content in a compelling manner, without sacrificing 
server performance.  RealAudio and other multimedia applications, 
require substantial server bandwidth and processing power to service  
heavy-user demand.  Recent WebStone benchmarks 
(http://www.digital.com/info/alphaserver/news/1perf.html) clearly 
show Alpha's 64-bit performance as the best choice to meet these 
demands.  

     MCI's electronic commerce music Web site was the first to offer 
RealAudio server capabilities from a Digital AlphaServer. 
"www.1800musicnow.com is considered by many audiophiles to be one of 
the best music-based sites on the Web," noted Brad Carlson, 
director, NetworkMCI Services for MCI. "A big reason for that is the 
speed and reliability of the AlphaServer, combined with the advanced 
features of Progressive Networks' RealAudio."

     Progressive Networks' RealAudio client/server software system 
enables Internet and online users equipped with conventional 
multimedia personal computers and voice-grade telephone lines to 
browse, select and play back audio or audio-based multimedia content 
on demand, in real time.  This is a breakthrough compared to 
conventional online methods in which audio is downloaded at a rate 
that is five times longer than the actual program, requiring the 
listener to wait 25 minutes to listen to five minutes of audio.  
Since its introduction last April, over five million RealAudio 
Players have been distributed, with over 25,000 being downloaded 
from the RealAudio Web site daily.  

     Progressive Networks, based in Seattle, develops and markets 
software products and services designed to enable users of personal 
computers and other digital devices to send and receive audio and 
audio-based multimedia services using the existing infrastructure.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  
