              Digital Announces New StorageWorks Array
                  Controllers for OpenVMS Customers


  Up to 50% performance boost for transaction-oriented applications


MAYNARD, Mass., August 14, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a new generation of high-performance StorageWorks 
array controllers for OpenVMS customers using Digital's Cluster 
Interconnect (CI) or Digital's Small Systems Interconnect (DSSI) 
platforms on Alpha or VAX systems.

     The new HSJ50 and HSD50 controllers provide impressive 
performance gains that can be measured in dramatically reduced 
response time to end users. Performance-boosting features include 
the power of 128MB writeback cache and an upgraded controller 
design. In addition, customers with first-generation HSJ and HSD 
30/40 controllers can supercharge their performance with an easy 
HSJ50 or HSD50 upgrade.

     "We're providing our StorageWorks customers with a big jump in 
performance with these controllers, and making it easy and cost-
effective for them to upgrade," said Larry Huber, Array Controller 
marketing manager for Digital.

The HSJ50 for CI Environments

     The HSJ50 array controllers for CI platforms offer a 300% 
improvement in I/O rates over the HSJ40 family. Bandwidth also jumps 
200%, and block transfers double in size. Such improvements in I/O 
performance are significant to users of high-volume database or 
transaction processing applications. Bandwidth impacts the 
performance of applications that transfer large blocks of data, 
including data warehousing or decision support.

     "The performance enhancements resulting from the larger cache 
sizes and block transfers mean that existing workloads can be run in 
much less time," said Huber. "For transaction-oriented applications, 
this means response time can be reduced by as much as 50%."

The HSD50 for DSSI Environments

     With the HSD50 controllers, twice as many devices are supported 
per controller. Bandwidth is also improved by 35% over the HSD30 
controller family. The capacity of each DSSI bus can be nearly 
doubled without changing or purchasing adapters, making this an 
ideal solution for applications that require more storage capacity 
but have maximized the adapters and quantity of supported DSSI 
buses. The HSD50 can be installed in place of an RF disk drive, 
HSD05 or HSD10 controller.

     The new writeback cache design allows up to 128MB per HSJ50 or 
HSD50 controller, assuring customers higher levels of both read and 
write performance. The larger cache availability also supports 
maximum I/O performance for future larger disk drives.

     Disk partitioning, which allows system managers to allocate 
capacity where it is needed, is also a standard feature on both the 
HSJ50 and HSD50 array controllers, as is RAID. StorageWorks array 
controllers adaptive RAID 3/5, providing excellent performance 
across a broad range of application types.

     Universal cache is another StorageWorks design feature of both 
the HSJ and HSD array controller families. The implementation of 
universal cache means that a controller's cache is available to all 
devices attached to that controller, and an external cache battery 
in the StorageWorks building blocks is also standard. Users can 
easily observe fault indicator lights and perform their own battery 
replacement.

Easy Upgrade Program

     Digital is offering an easy upgrade program to give OpenVMS 
customers a cost-effective way to start reaping the performance 
benefits of the new HSJ50 and HSD50 array controllers -- with a 
single part number on a purchase order and one low price for 
exchange/upgrade. Upgrades are available immediately, starting at 
$11,000 for the HSD50 family and $19,000 for the HSJ50 family.

     "We're offering a 30-day period for returning the old 
controller, which makes it easy to schedule on-site installation of 
the second-generation HSJ50 or HSD50 modules," Huber explained.

     For more information on StorageWorks array controllers or 
Digital's complete line of storage hardware and software products, 
call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) or visit 
http://www.storage.digital.com on the Worldwide web.

