         Improved Parallel Capabilities For Gaussian 94 
            on Digital's 64-Bit AlphaServer Systems 
            Leads to Enhanced Modeling Capabilities


Orlando, FLA -- August 26, 1996 -- Gaussian, Inc., today announced 
substantially increased parallel execution capabilities for its 
Gaussian 94 electronic structure program running on high-performance 
64-bit multiprocessor AlphaServer systems from Digital Equipment 
Corporation. These enhancements are the result of a comprehensive 
development initiative between the two companies.

Previous releases of Gaussian 94 included parallel energy 
calculations, geometry optimizations and prediction of vibrational 
frequencies for the Hartree-Fock and Density Functional Theory (DFT) 
methods for shared memory multiprocessor systems.

This latest release (revision D.4) incorporates an efficient 
parallel matrix multiplication facility, created by Digital, within 
the program. This addition enables the extremely accurate modeling 
required by chemists and chemical engineers, using the Quadratic 
Configuration Interaction (QCI) methods, to be performed in parallel 
on Digital's 64-bit multiprocessing AlphaServer systems. 
Parallelization makes these highly accurate models applicable to 
significantly larger molecules than was possible before.

Digital's AlphaServer family of systems is the industry's only 
complete line of tested, proven and mature high performance 64-bit 
RISC servers, ranging from the AlphaServer 8400 enterprise server, 
to the AlphaServer 4100 midrange server, to the AlphaServer 2100 
departmental server. 

"With the combination of Gaussian 94 and Digital's 64-bit 
AlphaServer systems, chemists can study the very large problems of 
commercial and scientific interest at high performance levels," said 
Mike Frisch, president of Gaussian, Inc. "The new parallel QCI 
features in the latest release of Gaussian 94 will be of great 
benefit to our mutual customers," Frisch continued.

"We are pleased to extend our relationship with Gaussian, Inc.," 
said Herb Shumway, vice president of Digital's Software Partners 
Group. "Digital stands alone in the industry today in the ability to 
deliver complete 64-bit solutions to customers, and the enhanced 
proficiency of this latest release of Gaussian 94 showcases the 
proven performance capabilities of Digital's AlphaServer systems in 
the demanding computational chemistry environment."

About Gaussian 94

In addition to enabling larger molecular systems to be studied with 
existing methods, Gaussian 94 allows many new properties to be 
computed for the first time in a commercially available package. Its 
most important new capabilities include the following:

     * 	Prediction of NMR spectra and chemical shifts.

     * 	General solvation models, including the Self-Consistent 
        Isodensity Polarized Continuum Model (SCI-PCM), allowing 
        chemical species to be studied in their natural state rather 
        than being approximated (often poorly) via the gas phase.

     * 	Highly efficient optimizations of ground states and 
        transition structures.

     * 	Automated high accuracy energies for computing 
        thermochemical properties, including the Gaussian-1 (G1) and 
        Gaussian-2 theories and variants (G2 and G2(MP2)) and the 
        Complete Basis Set (CBS) methods.

About Gaussian, Inc.

Gaussian, Inc. develops, sells and supports the Gaussian series of 
electronic structure programs. Gaussian is available for every major 
computing environment, from PC's to supercomputers, and it is 
currently used in a wide variety of industrial, governmental and 
academic research settings worldwide. Founded in 1987, Gaussian, 
Inc. is a privately-held company headquartered in Pittsburgh, PA. 
The company is also developing other, related software for chemists.

About Digital

Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
