        Digital Announces Record-breaking SAP R/3 Performance
                           For Windows NT


        ... AlphaServer 4100 claims R/3 performance lead ...


PHILADELPHIA -- August 26, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, 
winner of SAP America's 1996 "Award of Excellence," announced that 
its new AlphaServer 4100 5/400 system has achieved record-breaking 
performance for SAP R/3 Sales and Distribution (SD) benchmark for a 
Microsoft Windows NT environment. Digital unveiled these compelling 
results here today at SAPphire, the SAP users' conference. 

     The benchmark environment was a four-processor AlphaServer 4100 
5/400 system, which will begin shipping in September, with 4 GB of 
main memory and 66 GB of total disk space running Windows NT 3.51, 
Oracle7 Enterprise Server V7.2.2, and R/3 Rel. 3.0D.

     The benchmark achieved throughput of 49,300 dialog steps per 
hour with an average dialog response time of 1.68 sec. A total of 
160 SD benchmark users was measured. The throughput is equal to 822 
SAPS*. The average CPU utilization was 99 percent. This benchmark 
fully complies WITH SAP`s stringent benchmark regulations and has 
been audited and certified by SAP.

Alpha Powers Superior Windows NT Performance

     The new AlphaServer 4100 5/400 offers up to four 400 MHz Alpha 
64-bit microprocessors, the world's fastest, providing unmatched 
throughput, scalability, and flexibility. For even greater levels of 
availability, performance, and affordability, the system can be 
clustered with any other AlphaServer system. It also offers the 
industry's first 64-bit PCI I/O subsystem, providing up to 500 
MB/sec. of bandwidth. This ensures balanced system performance while 
taking advantage of industry-standard PCI options. 

     The new system drawer design and choice of pedestal or 
small-footprint cabinet models provide mix-and-match, rack-and-stack 
flexibility for meeting customers' current and future technology and 
business needs.

Unique Choice of Platforms for R/3 on Windows NT

     "Only Digital offers customers the choice of Alpha or Intel for 
running R/3 on Windows NT," said Toni Steiner, Digital`s Worldwide 
SAP Business Director. "In fact, Digital's AlphaServer systems are 
the only RISC platform supporting SAP`s R/3 system for Microsoft 
Windows NT. Further, with Alpha, customers can switch from UNIX to 
Windows NT, or vise versa, without changing the hardware platform."

     Steiner added, "More and more customers ask for Windows NT for 
large R/3 implementations. For customers that plan to roll out R/3 
company-wide based on Windows NT, Alpha with Windows NT is the right 
choice. They get performance and scalability they need today, and 
they benefit from the strategic alliance between Digital and 
Microsoft."

     Recently Microsoft Corp. said it intends to support 64-bit data 
in the Windows NT operating system to meet the needs of customers 
who require efficient access to extremely large databases. This 
functionality will be supported initially on Digital's Alpha 
platforms.

     The SAP benchmark was conducted at Digital`s SAP Technology 
Center in Viernheim, Germany. Technical details regarding the 
benchmark are available upon request from SAP AG or Digital.

     For more information, see the AlphaServer WWW site 
http://www.digital.com/info/alphaserver.  For more information on 
SAP AG see WWW site http://www.sap.com

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
                                ####

Note to Editors:  Digital, AlphaServer, and the Digital logo are 
                  trademarks of Digital Equipment Corporation. SAP 
                  is a trademark of SAP AG. Oracle7 is a registered 
                  trademark of Oracle Corporation. Windows NT is a 
                  trademark of Microsoft Corporation. 
     		  *  SAPS  =  SAP Application Benchmark Performance 
                  Standard. 100 SAPS are defined as 2,000 fully 
                  business processed order line items per hour in 
                  the Standard SD benchmark. This is equivalent to 
                  6,000 dialog steps and 2,000 postings per hour, or 
                  2,400 SAP transactions per hour.


