            Digital Announces Altavista Internet Security
                    Products For Intel Platforms


        AltaVista Firewall and AltaVista Tunnel now available
                      on Windows NT and BSD/OS


MAYNARD, Mass., August 28, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new members of the AltaVista Security family -- 
industrial-strength Tunnel and Firewall products on Intel platforms.   
These products implement the AltaVista OnSite Computing vision, 
which enables cyberworkers to access critical business information 
from any location at any time. AltaVista Security products allow 
users to simply and cost-effectively protect private networks from 
the Internet and create secure Virtual Private Networks (VPN) over 
the Internet.  In addition, the company announced that AltaVista 
Firewall has been certified by the National Computing Security
Association (NCSA) as the industry's first approved firewall on 
Windows NT.

     "We're pleased to offer the simplicity and security of the 
respected AltaVista Firewall and AltaVista Tunnel products on both 
Intel and Alpha platforms," said Ilene H. Lang, vice president of 
Digital's Internet Software Business Unit.  "As the only provider of 
an NCSA-certified firewall for Windows NT, we are proud that users 
of the AltaVista Firewall can be assured that their security system 
meets one of the highest, independent, industry standards."

     "I thought the UNIX version of AltaVista Firewall was the 
easiest, most secure firewall we could set up. The NT version is 
easier still.  The market wants this product," said Dave Backstrom, 
president of Vital Integration Solutions, Inc., West Des Moines, 
Iowa.  "The user-tiered pricing for AltaVista Firewall (NT) makes 
the best product in the industry affordable for the little guy."

     According to Philip DeLeon, president of Onyx Computers, 
Richmond Hill, Ontario, a reseller of AltaVista products, "The best 
just got better.  With Digital announcing AltaVista Firewall and 
AltaVista Tunnel support for Windows NT and BSD/OS, our Intel and 
Alpha customers can now incorporate state-of-the-art secure 
technology into their private networks with peace of mind."

AltaVista Tunnel for Windows NT, BSD/OS, FreeBSD and Digital UNIX

     AltaVista Tunnel combines authentication, encryption and a 
unique firewall-independent design to provide highly secure and 
cost-effective remote access for telecommuters, mobile workers and 
branch offices. Remote-based individuals or members of remote LANs 
and WANs can securely communicate and share information with 
individuals and groups on a company Intranets without the expense of 
leased lines, modem banks, 800 numbers or long distance dial-up 
access.

AltaVista Firewall for Windows NT, BSD/OS and Digital UNIX

     The NCSA-Certified AltaVista Firewall deploys a unique 
combination of technologies that place a highly-secure, yet flexible 
barrier between private networks, the Internet and other private 
networks.  

AltaVista Firewall runs on Windows NT, BSD/OS and Digital UNIX and 
is based on technology used by Digital in its own Internet firewalls 
for almost 10 years.  It combines trusted application gateways, 
comprehensive logging, real-time reporting, evasive action and a 
easy-to-use GUI.

Pricing and Availability

AltaVista Firewall for Windows NT and BSD/OS will be available on 
August 30, 1996. Pricing is as follows:

     *	$3,995 for 50 users
