         Digital Brings Newest Microsoft Windows Solutions
                                  
                         To The Enterprise
                                  

             Company Delivers Industry's Broadest Line
         of Servers and Client PCs Ready for Windows NT 4.0
                                  
     MAYNARD, Mass., July 31, 1996 -- Continuing its leadership 
position in providing enterprise Windows NT-based solutions, 
Digital Equipment Corporation today announced support for Microsoft 
Windows NT version 4.0 across its server, workstation, desktop PC, 
and notebook computer lines.  In addition, Digital announced that 
it will ship the new Microsoft Windows 95 OEM Service Release 2.0 
on its desktop and notebook systems.  Digital is rolling out the 
new releases as they become available from Microsoft Corp.

     The combination of Digital's scalable range of reliable, 
high-performance Intel and Alpha platforms and the easy-to-use, 
robust Microsoft Windows operating systems provides enterprise 
customers with the most highly available, most cost-effective, and 
most manageable computing solutions.

     "Digital delivers the greatest choice of Windows-certified 
servers and clients, plus value-added software, and worldwide 
service and support -- all backed by our strategic relationship 
with Microsoft, the Alliance for Enterprise Computing," said Bruce 
Claflin, vice president and general manager of Digital's Personal 
Computer Business Unit.  "Microsoft's new releases of Windows NT 
and Windows 95 will bring new advantages to customers at every 
level of client/server computing, and Digital leads the way in 
enabling enterprise customers to make the most of those benefits."

     "The new releases of Windows announced by Microsoft today are 
well complemented by Digital's extensive array of Windows-focused 
platforms and solutions," said Jim Allchin, senior vice president 
for the desktop and business systems division at Microsoft.  "We 
are pleased that Digital has chosen Windows NT and Windows 95 to 
complement its broad product offerings to help business customers 
tap the full benefits of Windows-based computing."

     Enterprise-class customers will benefit from innovations 
introduced in Microsoft's latest releases of Windows NT and Windows 
95, including unprecedented ease of use, a user interface common to 
Windows NT and Windows 95, and built-in Internet and Intranet 
capabilities.
Widest Choice of Servers and Clients for Windows NT 4.0

     Digital's Intel and Alpha-based servers and client PCs are 
certified for use with Windows NT 4.0.  These systems range from 
Prioris servers and AlphaServer systems; to the AlphaStation 
family, the industry's fastest desktops; to Digital's Intel and 
Alpha-based Personal Workstations; to the Celebris and Venturis 
commercial desktop PCs; to the HiNote Ultra II, the market's 
thinnest and lightest full-function Pentium notebook.  Advancing 
its lead in making it easier to deploy and use Windows NT on 
enterprise clients, Digital will also preconfigure models of its 
personal workstations, desktops, and notebooks with Windows NT 4.0.
Servers Lead in Performance, Availability, Manageability

     Windows NT Server 4.0 will be available for Digital's 
powerful, Pentium Pro and Pentium-based Prioris servers and for its 
high-performance AlphaServer systems.  The Prioris and AlphaServer 
lines offer a range of processing power that scales from workgroup 
applications through enterprise-class servers.  They combine 
superior performance, cost-of-ownership, expandability, and 
robustness with advanced manageability through Digital's 
ServerWORKS software.  For even higher levels of availability, 
Prioris and AlphaServer systems are available with Digital Clusters 
for Windows NT -- the industry's premiere high availability 
clustered solution for Windows NT Server.

     Digital's Prioris ZX 6166MP/4 server shatters the performance 
record for a Pentium Pro server running Windows NT 4.0 and MS SQL 
Server 6.5.  In recent TPC-C benchmark testing, the four-way 
symmetric multiprocessing Prioris ZX server achieved results of 
5,740 tpmC at an unprecedented $116.93 per tpmC, topping the 
previous record set by Compaq Computer Corporations ProLiant 5000 
system.

     Breakthrough levels of performance and cost-effectiveness for 
Windows NT Server are extended even further by Digital's 
AlphaServer family of RISC-based systems, which are powered by the 
world's fastest microprocessors, including the AlphaServer 400, 
1000, and 2100 lines and the new AlphaServer 4100 system.
Clients Ready for Newest Releases of Windows NT and Windows 95

     Digital will preload the newest release of Windows NT and the 
OEM update to Windows 95 on newly manufactured models of its client 
PCs, workstations, and notebooks.

     - Digital's Personal Workstations will be available with 
       Windows NT Workstation 4.0 preinstalled.  The industry's 
       fastest personal workstations, the family features a 
       processor-independent design that enables fast and easy 
       upgrades to the latest Pentium Pro and Digital Alpha 
       processors.  Digital AlphaStation systems push performance 
       levels even higher for Windows NT 4.0.  The AlphaStation 
       family provides a choice of Windows NT, OpenVMS, or UNIX.

     - A choice of Windows NT 4.0 or the OEM update to Windows 95 
       will be available preloaded on Digital's commercial desktop 
       PCs, including models from the Celebris and Venturis desktop 
       PC families.  The OEM update to Windows 95 will be available 
       on Digital's price/performance leading Venturis FX line of 
       Pentium desktop PCs.  Celebris and Venturis systems make it 
       easier for enterprises to manage their client PCs with 
       Digital's industry-standard ClientWORKS software.  
       ClientWORKS is included at no additional charge on all of 
       Digital's desktop and mobile systems.

     - Continuing its leadership in Windows NT for the mobile 
       professional, Digital is one of the first to offer Windows 
       NT 4.0 on a mobile system.  Digital will not only preload 
       Windows NT 4.0 on selected models of the HiNote Ultra II, it 
       will introduce enhanced docking support for system options 
       and a broader range of peripherals, and add new power 
       management features that extend battery life.  The OEM 
       update to Windows 95 will be available across future models 
       of Digital's notebooks, the HiNote Ultra II and the HiNote 
       VP mobile clients.

     Digital's solutions are the leading choice for customers 
deploying Windows NT across the enterprise.  Digital offers 
enterprise customers superior value with client/server solutions 
optimized for Windows and Windows NT, global services and support, 
and solutions delivered through alliances with industry leaders.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

