      Digital Announces Object Technology Software Agreements
                    with Rational and I-Kinetics
                                  
	 MAYNARD, Mass., August 5, 1996 --- Digital Equipment
Corporation today announced object-oriented technology agreements 
with industry-leading software vendors Rational Software 
Corporation of Santa Clara, California and I-Kinetics of 
Burlington, Massachusetts which will significantly enhance 
Digital's overall object technology solution portfolio.

	 Digital and Rational have integrated the Rational Rose 
object-oriented analysis and development software with 
ObjectBroker. Rational Rose will enable users to easily create
OMG IDL (interface definition language) models in Rational's 
Rose, and supply the generated IDL code directly to 
ObjectBroker's QuickStart tool for the creation of elegant 
client and server applications.

	 "Rational Rose and ObjectBroker create an unbeatable
combination of best-in-class object-oriented development and
CORBA middleware for simplified, yet production-quality,
multi-platform distributed computing," says Erik Townsend,
president of The Cushing Group, a leader in distributed object
consulting and training, based in Nashua, New Hampshire.

	 For CORBA development that ties into relational
databases, I-Kinetics' Database Component Server will be working
with ObjectBroker to greatly reduce the need for developers to 
write interface code to their favorite databases.

	 The Database Component Server V3.0 is for CORBA 
developers who need a "brokerage service" to access a variety of
databases. Unlike class libraries and mapping tools, the Database
Component Server is plug-and-play. It presents databases as fully
functional CORBA objects which can be installed and used right
out of the box. The Database Component Server works with Oracle
and Sybase databases.

	 Demonstrations of both the Rational Rose and I-Kinetics 
Database Component Server connection to ObjectBroker will be
available in the Digital booth (#716) at Object World West in San 
Jose, California (August 20-22, 1996).

	 Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in
open client/server solutions from personal computing to 
integrated worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and
Alpha platforms, storage, networking, software and services,
together with industry-focused solutions from business 
partners, help organizations compete and win in today's global
marketplace.
