                 Digital's HiNote Ultra II Packs More Punch

                  New Model Available with Intel's Latest, 
               Fastest Pentium Processor for Mobile Computing

     MAYNARD, Mass., Aug. 5, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the latest addition to its award-winning HiNote line 
of mobile client solutions for the corporate enterprise.  The new 
Digital HiNote Ultra II model LTS5150 incorporates Intel's brand new 
150-megahertz (MHz) Pentium processor designed specifically for 
high-performance mobile computers.  The system has a suggested
list price of U.S. $5,099 and is among the first notebooks using 
this technology to be available in the commercial market worldwide.

     "Our goal is to provide our corporate customers the benefit of 
the latest technology for increasing the productivity of their 
mobile clients while maximizing their investment protection," said 
Howard Elias, vice president of worldwide business segments in 
Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit. "With today's 
announcement of the Ultra II LTS5150, we're acting quickly and
aggressively to continue our market leadership in delivering truly 
mobile solutions that respond to customer needs for maximum value 
and performance."

Continued Industry Leadership in Thin and Light

     Digital's new HiNote Ultra II -- still the thinnest, lightest 
and among the fastest Pentium notebooks on the market -- includes 
many industry-leading features in the lightweight, ultraportable 
category.  For increased performance, the system includes 16 
megabytes of standard system memory, 256 kilobytes of external cache 
memory and accelerated local-bus graphics.  A large, 11.3-inch SVGA 
(Super Video Graphics Array) color display with active-matrix 
technology delivers bright, crisp graphical images for exciting
visual presentations.  The HiNote Ultra II LTS5150 features a 
removable hard drive with 1.44 gigabytes of storage for support of 
the most demanding mobile applications.  An optional 6X-speed CD-ROM 
and stereo speaker module -- the HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module -- 
is also available for fully integrated multimedia capabilities.

     "Digital continues to push the envelope in ergonomic design,
user-friendly integration and leading-edge technology to bring 
mobile professionals the ultimate in portability," said Stephen 
Nachtsheim, vice president of Intel's Mobile and Handheld Products 
Group.  "Powered by our new 150MHz Pentium processor, Digital's 
second-generation HiNote Ultra II continues to deliver truly 
no-compromise notebook solutions for mobile clients within the
enterprise."

Mobile Clients Built for the Windows Enterprise

     As Microsoft's Windows operating systems continue to lead the 
market as the most popular software platforms for the corporate 
environment, Digital continues to deliver industry-leading mobile 
client solutions built for the Windows enterprise.  Digital's HiNote 
Ultra II comes pre-loaded with Windows 95, currently the most 
popular operating system for mobile professionals. Models featuring 
Windows for Workgroups 3.11 are also available.

     As Windows NT further establishes itself as the fastest growing 
network operating system, Digital maintains its Windows NT 
leadership position in the mobile arena with pre-loaded Windows NT 
mobile clients.  The entire line of HiNote Ultra II notebooks is 
available with Windows NT pre-loaded and pre-configured to run 
straight from the box.  This saves customers the time and manpower 
typically necessary to install and configure Windows NT-based mobile
systems and options, significantly reducing the cost of implementing 
mobile solutions within a Windows NT environment.

     Windows NT 3.51 is currently shipping on the HiNote Ultra II 
line, with Digital-enhanced features including easy docking of 
system options such as the HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module and 
selected PC Card peripherals.  The company plans to offer the 
recently announced Windows NT Version 4.0 as soon as it is available 
from Microsoft.  Digital's pre-configured Windows NT 4.0 notebook
solutions will provide increased functionality for the mobile 
client, such as enhanced docking support for system options and a 
broader range of peripherals, and new power management features for 
extended battery life.

Pricing and Availability

     Digital's HiNote family is targeted at customers from the small 
office business user to sophisticated, large business mobile 
professionals.  The HiNote Ultra II model LTS5150 is available 
immediately worldwide through Digital's channel partners and 
authorized resellers with a suggested list price of U.S. $5,099.  
The HiNote Ultra II model LTS5150 with Windows NT is available on a 
special-order basis at a suggested list price of U.S. $5,299.  
Digital's HiNote Ultra II notebook family comes with a three-year 
warranty including one year of the company's next-day, on-site 
Passport Service.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

