               Digital Semiconductor Teams with Partners
               to Show Alpha Visual Computing Leadership

              ...Windows NT Performance, Compatibility
                    Highlight SIGGRAPH Exhibit...
                                  
		        SIGGRAPH '96 Booth 74

     NEW ORLEANS, August 6, 1996 -- Alpha performance leadership 
for the visual computing industry's most popular Windows NT 
applications headlines the exhibit by Digital Semiconductor, a 
Digital Equipment Corporation business, in Booth 740 at SIGGRAPH 
'96 at the Ernest N. Morial Convention Center.

     Digital Semiconductor's exhibit focuses on high performance 
visual computing applications for video editing, 3-D image 
rendering and animation, as well as a broad selection of Windows NT 
software used in the video, film, and multimedia production 
industries.  Eleven Alpha system manufacturers are also showing 
their latest systems in Booth 740, and Digital Semiconductor is 
again sponsoring its annual Alpha PC Giveaway, offering show-goers 
a chance to win an Alpha multimedia personal computer.
Picking the Performance Leader

     To compare Alpha performance with other leading architectures, 
a system based on an Alpha 21164-466MHz microprocessor competes 
against Silicon Graphics' Indigo II workstation, based on the MIPS 
R4400 chip at 250MHz, and Intergraph's TDZ-400 workstation using 
two 200MHz Pentium Pro processors.  Relative performance of image 
rendering, using Microsoft's SOFTIMAGE 3D and NewTek's Lightwave 3D 
4.0 application software, is demonstrated, and elapsed times are 
posted for each system.

Compatibility -- The Differentiator

     Digital FX!32 software, Digital's unique binary translator 
that enables Alpha systems to run the entire portfolio of 32-bit 
Windows applications, is featured in a "test drive" comparing the 
performance of 466MHz Alpha systems to 200MHz Pentium Pro systems.  
The demonstration uses popular applications such as Adobe 
Photoshop, Microsoft Office 95, CORELDRAW, and a selection of games 
to show how Alpha with Digital FX!32 software is the only RISC 
processsor that equals or surpasses Pentium and Pentium Pro 
performance in the most widely used WIN32 applications.
Partner Pavilion

     Booth 740's Alpha Partner Pavilion highlights the latest Alpha 
solutions and demonstrations by 11 of Digital Semiconductor's Alpha 
partners (see accompanying press releases).  They are:

  *   Aspen Systems, Inc.					   
  *   Carrera Computers, Inc.
  *   Core Microsystems, Inc.					   
  *   DeskStation Technology, Inc.
  *   Eye-On Software, Inc.					   
  *   Microway, Inc.
  *   Panda Project, Inc.					   
  *   Parallex
  *   Polywell Computers, Inc.					   
  *   Rare Systems, Inc.
  *   StarMedia Systems
     
     "The presence of a growing number of Alpha system vendors in 
the video editing and animation markets proves that Alpha is the 
best microprocessor architecture for visual computing," said Tim 
Miller, Digital Semiconductor's Alpha strategic marketing manager.  
"Further, with Digital FX!32 software, you can have Alpha's image 
rendering speed without sacrificing performance or access to the 
full repertory of 32-bit Windows applications."

Win an Alpha PC

     Visitors to the Digital Semiconductor booth receive directions 
for participation in the drawing for a free Alpha PC.  By attending 
Alpha demonstrations, participants can qualify for a free Alpha 
T-shirt and entry for the drawing, which will be held on the last 
day of the show.

     Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment Corporation 
business headquartered in Hudson, Massachusetts, designs, 
manufactures and markets industry-leading semiconductor products 
including Alpha microprocessors and PCI chips for networking, 
bridging, and multimedia, plus low-power StrongARM microprocessors 
under license from Advanced RISC Machines Ltd.  Mitsubishi Electric 
Corporation and Samsung Electronics Company Ltd. are alternate 
sources for Alpha microprocessors.  World Wide Web site:  
http://www.digital.com/info/semiconductor

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

