            Digital Animates Windows NT at SIGGRAPH '96


                          SIGGRAPH '96
                           Booth# 805


NEW ORLEANS, LA, August 6, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation is
strengthening its presence in the entertainment market with the 
industry's premier Windows NT-based workstations, servers, and 
popular software solutions from partners, as showcased at SIGGRAPH 
'96. Digital is also re-asserting its graphics leadership in both 
the UNIX and Windows NT markets with the following announcements 
(see separate press releases): 

     o 	three new graphics adapters -- the PowerStorm 4D40T, 4D50T, 
        and 4D60T -- which provide high-performance 3D features and 
        advanced texture mapping at unmatched prices 

     o 	a 500 MHz version of the AlphaStation 500 workstation, a 
        system that delivers the highest integer and floating point 
        performance of any desktop workstation on the market.  

     o 	an alliance with Evans and Sutherland through which E&S will 
        provide extremely high-end graphics under the Windows NT 
        operating system

     "The incredible number of Windows NT-based personal 
workstations at SIGGRAPH '96 is evidence of a paradigm shift in the 
computer graphics industry away from traditional UNIX systems," said 
Philippe Ribeyre, vice president Digital's Workstations Business 
Unit. "Digital plans to gain significant mindshare and marketshare 
in this industry with its revolutionary Windows NT Intel- and 
Alpha-based personal workstations, leading high-performance 3D 
PowerStorm graphics adapters, and partnerships with innovative 
software companies." 

Products on Display

     Customers can get a first look at newly announced products
including three new PowerStorm adapters and the AlphaStation 500/500
workstation. Together, the PowerStorm graphics adapters and the
AlphaStation 500/500 workstation offer up to 45 percent better 
graphics performance than SGI's High Impact workstation. The Alpha 
XL 366 personal workstation, announced this Spring, is also on 
display at Siggraph '96.  This high-performance workstation offers 
23 percent more floating point and 12 percent better graphics 
performance than SGI's High Impact workstation for half the price. 

     Digital is also running a technical demonstration of its 
yet-to-be-announced Pentium Pro workstation.  

Windows NT Solutions for Digital Content Creation and 
Post-Production

     At the show, Digital is demonstrating applications from key
partners on its Intel- and Alpha-based workstations that video 
producers and games developers use for content creation and 
post-production. 

     Animation packages on display include Microsoft's Softimage 3D 
and NewTek's LightWave 3D for Alpha systems, and Knitex's 3D Studio 
Max for Intel systems. Post-production software includes Avid's 
Elastic Reality for special effects and morphing and MCXpress for 
non-linear video editing.  This software and Digital's Windows 
NT-based workstations bring low-cost, high-performance animation and 
post-production solutions to animation, post, and special-effects 
houses, as well as film studios. 

     For real-time games development and delivery, Digital is 
featuring a unique solution comprised of MultiGen's GameGen II, Data 
Path's RealiMation, Mak Technologies' VRLink, and 3Dfx Interactive's 
Obsidian Pro and AccelGraphics' AGPro 2000 graphics adapters. With 
this solution, developers can easily develop games in real time and 
can efficiently deploy them for PCs, console-game platforms, 
arcades, and location-based entertainment. 

Animating the WEB

     Digital is demonstrating how Alpha animates the WEB with 
Windows NT, enabling animators to be more productive and creative at 
a fraction of the cost associated with other vendors' systems. 
Digital and Integrated Data Systems (IDS) have created a 3D VRML WEB 
page using IDS's VRealm software to showcase the animation 
capabilities of Digital's Windows NT-based workstations and servers. 
The demonstration moves the audience through an animated VRML world. 
Customers can move through this virtual-reality world on their own 
using an Alpha XL 300 running Softimage or a Celebris XL personal 
workstation with 3D Studio MAX. Digital's Windows NT-based 
workstations and PowerStorm graphics bring ease-of-use and low
cost of ownership to this emerging market. 

Highest Rendering Performance

     Digital is also demonstrating the highest rendering performance 
in the industry. An AlphaServer 4100 system running Digital UNIX and 
another running Windows NT go head to head against an SGI Power 
Challenge L server.  The servers handle rendering tasks and the 
clients, an SGI Indigo2 workstation and an AlphaStation 500/500, 
perform animation.  Digital's UNIX-based server performs rendering 
four times faster than the SGI system, both running Pixar's 
Renderman software.  Digital's Windows NT server running Microsoft's 
Mental Ray software performs rendering three times faster. The 
workstations and demonstrate Digital's seamless UNIX-to-Windows NT 
interoperability in a networked environment that is unmatched in 
the industry. 

Miracle Factory Chooses Digital and Windows NT for Animation

     Burton Marcus, the chairman of Miracle Factory, a digital
application and design studio that specializes in 2D and 3D 
animation for television, books, training, education, and the 
internet, said he sees the future with Digital and Windows NT-based 
solutions. Miracle Factory purchased 35 AlphaStation 500/333 
workstations and two AlphaServer 4100 systems after extensive 
research. The systems will network the entire company, located in 
the heart of New York City's entertainment district, and will run 
UNIX and Windows NT animation applications, including Microsoft's 
Softimage and Toon Boom Technologies' Tic Tac Tune software. 

     "Animation is an iterative process--the faster the job runs the
lower the production costs," Marcus said. "Digital has always had
exceptional products. Now the company is making a good move by 
focusing on Windows NT because everyone will eventually use it and 
Digital is one of the only companies that has formed a strategic 
alliance with Microsoft.  Digital provides seamless communication 
between UNIX and Windows NT systems. Because of the amazing speed of 
Alpha and outstanding connectivity with Windows NT, Digital is in a 
position to occupy this market." 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.


                   SOLUTIONS FROM LEADING PARTNERS

     


Digital is showcasing its workstations and servers with a wide range 
of hardware and software solutions for the entertainment market on
the show floor in the Digital Booth #805, and in partners' own 
booths, including: 

Digital Semiconductor (Booth #1730) -- Digital Semiconductor is  
showing an AlphaStation 500/500 workstation running Windows NT and 
Softimage.

Eyeon Software, Inc. (Booth #SP4) -- Eyeon Software, Inc. is
presenting Digital Fusion NT, an advanced resolution independent
composting, image processing, and special effects tool for film and 
video production. 

Intel Corporation (Both #919) -- Intel is showcasing Digital 
Personal Workstations running leading applications for the 
entertainment industry.

Kinetix (Booth #819) -- Kinetix is revolutionizing 3D graphics on 
the PC with 3D Studio MAX.

Lucent Technology Software Solutions Group (Booth #403) -- Lucent is
showing Multimedia Designer for Windows NT, a 32-bit graphic design
software application for creating high-impact, photo-realistic 
images. 

MultiGen, Inc. (Booth #1929) -- MultiGen develops a leading realtime 
3D authoring software toolset for visual simulation, entertainment, 
and CAD visualization applications. MultiGen products are used to 
create, edit, optimize, and view realtime 3D scenes. MultiGen will 
feature SmartScene, MultiGen II Pro, GameGen II.

NewTek, Inc. (Booth #1656) -- NewTek's LightWave 3D has a 
comprehensive 3D feature set, providing workstation performance at 
PC prices. Due to its unparalleled rendering quality and case of 
use, LightWave 3D is the artist's choice for creating special 
effects for television, film, commercial, video game, and corporate 
applications. It is available for Windows 95 and NT on Intel and 
Alpha. 

Polhemus, Inc. (Booth #1705) -- Polhemus Fastrak is a highly-
accurate low latency 3D motion tracking and digitizing system. This 
award-winning system is the ultimate solution for realtime 
position/orientation sensing.

Portable Graphics, Inc. (Booth #217) -- Portable Graphics 
demonstrates Open Inventor for Windows NT and Digital UNIX on 
Digital's new PowerStorm 4D60T graphics accelerator featuring 
hardware-accelerated texture mapping. Open Inventor's 3D developer's 
toolkit is the emerging de facto standard for the development of 
high-performance, interactive 3D graphics applications.

Softimage/Microsoft (Booth #703/705) -- Softimage is featuring 
several of Digital's powerful AlphaStations and Digital Personal 
Workstations running Windows NT and Softimage 3.0. Digital's new 
PowerStorm 4D60T graphics accelerator with advanced text mapping for 
unparalleled performance is also included. 

Spaceward Graphics Limited (Booth #2706) -- The company is showing 
Satori Version 1.1 Resolution Independent Paint & 2D Graphics 
Software. This is a perfect companion for Adobe Photoship. It 
composites and edits large images using standard RAM configurations, 
delivering high-end workstation performance at a fraction of the 
cost. 

Template Graphics Software, Inc. (Booth #1029) -- Open Inventor for 
Win-32 is a C++3D/VRML toolkit for Windows NT/95. Visual 3Space 
Control is an ActiveX component for Visual Basic. 3Space Publisher 
is a Web page authoring product, and 3Space Assistant is a 3D 
desktop utility.

3Dfx Interactive, Inc. (Booth #2037) -- 3Dfx Interactive, Inc. 
develops 3D graphics products for the entertainment and visual 
simulation markets. The products consist of 3D graphics chips, 
accelerators, and software that enable users to manipulate objects 
and animation sequences in real time on an ordinary PC. These 3D 
products offer advanced features such as texture mapping and LOD 
MIP-mapping as well as unmatched triangle and fill-rate performance.
