        Digital and E&S Align to Bring Powerhouse Workstation
                       Graphics to Windows NT


NEW ORLEANS, LA, August 6, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and 
Evans & Sutherland today announced their intent to bring 
state-of-the-art 3D graphics technology from Evans & Sutherland to 
market on Digital's Alpha-based Windows NT workstations.  The 
alliance will bring a class of graphics workstation performance to 
Windows NT expected to exceed offerings from traditional UNIX 
graphics workstation vendors such as Silicon Graphics, Inc. 

     Evans & Sutherland, a proven leader and innovator in 3D 
graphics technology, announced earlier this year it would offer the 
next generation of high-end graphics products in the Windows NT 
environment. Today's announcement with Digital will set a new 
benchmark for image quality and performance. 

     "This announcement is an important step in the continuation of 
our strategy to provide the world's best graphics on the most 
cost-effective platform," said Jim Oyler, president and CEO of Evans 
& Sutherland.  "Our relationship with Digital is excellent and the 
combination of E&S graphics with Digital Alpha processors brings the 
highest standard of technology from both companies to Windows NT," 
he added. 

     "Digital's relationship with Evans & Sutherland ensures we will
have ultra high-end 3D graphics products and solutions on our Alpha
Windows NT workstations," said Philippe Ribeyre, vice president of
Digital's Workstation Business Segment.  "The rules of the graphics 
game have changed. The marketplace for graphics is moving rapidly to 
Windows NT and Digital will have the most comprehensive suite of 
Windows NT graphics accelerators available." 

     For Digital, this announcement complements the company's 
PowerStorm family of graphics adapters which include a full range of 
2D and 3D graphics offerings for both Windows NT and UNIX 
environments. 

     Digital expects to deliver the joint product early in 1997. 
Target markets include high-end automotive design and styling, 
animation, film and video production, and science and research. 

     E&S manufactures hardware and software for highly realistic 
visual systems that produce high-quality, 3D graphics and synthetic 
environments for a variety of simulation, entertainment, and virtual 
reality applications. E&S was founded in 1968 and is headquartered 
in the University of Utah Research Park, Salt Lake City, UT.  The 
E&S Homepage is located at http://www.es.com. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
