            Digital and BEA Team Up to Deliver a Jolt to
                         Electronic Commerce


        Provide Reliable, Secure, High-performance Processing
              of Business Transactions on the Internet


MAYNARD, Mass., August 6, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today announced that it is strengthening its support for Internet-
based electronic commerce by adding BEA Jolt, from BEA Systems, 
Inc., to its portfolio of Internet products and services.

     BEA Jolt enables customers to take advantage of the benefits of 
a BEA TUXEDO-based application over the "super-distributed" world of 
the Internet.  These benefits include: guaranteed delivery; time, 
location, and data independence; data-dependent routing; massive 
scalability; platform independence and legacy integration; load 
balancing; intelligent fail-over and recovery; and a single 
development API.  BEA Jolt has the added advantage of allowing 
companies to leverage their programming expertise so that Java 
programmers need know nothing of transaction semantics, and 
developers of mission-critical, transactional applications need not 
learn how to translate their code for the Internet.

     "As a leading expert in distributed, mission-critical 
computing, BEA is well qualified to provide the necessary infra-
structure to extend mission-critical computing to the Internet," 
said Don Harbert, vice president, UNIX Business Segment, Digital 
Equipment Corporation.  "The combination of Digital AlphaServer 
systems running Digital UNIX and BEA Jolt provides the performance 
and scalability to meet this challenge." 

     The BEA Distributed Application Framework with BEA TUXEDO
is the most widely available and widely used transaction processing 
framework supporting high-volume, mission-critical, distributed 
applications on open systems.  The framework provides the following 
capabilities for applications that must process the transactions 
that are of central importance to businesses:  scalability; 
transaction integrity at the server; support for all messaging 
paradigms; legacy and distributed system integration; and management 
and administration.

     "The combination of fast Digital 64-bit AlphaServer systems, 
capable of highly scalable clustering, and the robust BEA Jolt 
product, offers companies the first viable solution for setting up 
their businesses on the Internet," said Bill Coleman, chairman and 
CEO, BEA Systems, Inc.  "By making BEA TUXEDO available for the 
Internet through the addition of BEA Jolt running on AlphaServer 
systems, we have nearly instantaneously enabled a new class of 
Internet applications."

     Now, with the availability of BEA Jolt, the capabilities of the 
BEA Distributed Application Framework with BEA TUXEDO are available 
to Intranet clients of all types throughout the corporation and, 
optionally, to Internet clients beyond the corporation.  Any 
Intranet client device running Netscape Navigator, or other 
browsers supporting the Java Virtual Machine, can host an 
object-oriented client program (applet) written in Java that can 
invoke any existing or new BEA TUXEDO application server running 
anywhere on the corporate Intranet.  No special TP software needs to 
be installed on the client.

     The capabilities of the BEA Distributed Application Framework 
and BEA Jolt are complemented by Digital's AlphaServer systems 
running 64-bit Digital UNIX, which together enable faster access to 
data and information on the Internet.  In addition, users can take 
advantage of even greater scalability, availability and high 
performance with Digital UNIX TruCluster Solutions. 

     By adding Digital's AltaVista OnSite Access security products 
to their BEA Jolt environment, users are guaranteed a high degree of 
security for their communication over the Internet with AltaVista's 
encryption technology.  BEA plans to certify BEA Jolt with the 
AltaVista Tunnel and AltaVista Firewall products in the near future 
to enhance security for applications that span beyond the corporate 
Intranet. 

BEA Systems, Inc.

     BEA Systems, Inc., is the leading provider of distributed,
enterprise middleware solutions.  Founded in January 1995, BEA's
mission is to enable distributed mission-critical applications
that can seamlessly work with legacy, client/server, and now 
Internet environments.  BEA provides a Distributed Application
Framework, the infrastructure for developing and maintaining
distributed client/server applications, using the BEA TUXEDO
transactional and messaging middleware as its core engine.  BEA 
also provides professional services and will continue to build 
its solution through development, partnerships, and acquisitions.
Headquartered in Sunnyvale, Calif., BEA is venture funded by 
Warburg, Pincus Ventures, L.P.  Additional information on BEA is
available on the Internet at http://www.beasys.com

